	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Western Plaguelands were once the northern heartland of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}: a country of rolling farms, orchards, granaries and prosperous towns between the glades of {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal{/link} and the river that runs toward the east. Today they are a grey and poisoned land. The grass has withered, the trees stand bare, and the fields that fed a kingdom now feed only the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}. Great cauldrons breathe plague into the air above the old farmsteads. The dead walk the roads. Yet the land is not wholly lost. Three powers have come to contest it with the dead: the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} from the south, the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} from the west, and the {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link} from its stronghold in the north. None of them trusts the others.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records the year when these lands were first settled. They belonged to the kingdom of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} for as long as that kingdom stood, and they were among its richest. The city of {link:ruins-of-andorhal}Andorhal{/link} gathered the harvests of the north into its granaries. The town of {link:hearthglen}Hearthglen{/link} and the keep of Mardenholde guarded the northern hills, and in the years after the {link:second-war}Second War{/link} they were ruled by {link:tirion-fordring}Tirion Fordring{/link}, a lord and paladin of the Silver Hand. In the south, the Barov family held the island keep of {link:caer-darrow}Caer Darrow{/link} on its quiet lake, and the gentry of the kingdom went there to rest and to have their portraits painted by the water.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} rules the Western Plaguelands still. A lich called {link:araj-the-summoner}Araj the Summoner{/link} holds the ruins of {link:ruins-of-andorhal}Andorhal{/link}. Four plague cauldrons, tended by cauldron lords, poison the farmlands. In the south, beneath {link:caer-darrow}Caer Darrow{/link}, the cult trains its necromancers in the Scholomance.

Against them stand small forces at the edges of the land. At {link:chillwind-camp}Chillwind Camp{/link} in the south, {link:commander-ashlam-valorfist}Commander Ashlam Valorfist{/link} gathers the soldiers and champions of the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} under the banner of the {link:kingdom-of-stormwind}Kingdom of Stormwind{/link}. At the {link:the-bulwark}Bulwark{/link} in the west, {link:high-executor-derrington}High Executor Derrington{/link} holds the eastern gate of {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal{/link} for the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} and the {link:horde}Horde{/link}. In the north, the {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link} holds {link:hearthglen}Hearthglen{/link} under {link:taelan-fordring}Highlord Taelan Fordring{/link}. It fights the Scourge, and it fights everyone else as well. Agents of the {link:argent-dawn}Argent Dawn{/link} serve in both the Alliance and the Horde camps, and ask nothing of either but the war against the dead.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}.{/b} Skeletons, ghouls, abominations, wraiths and the restless spirits of the drowned and the slain. They hold {link:ruins-of-andorhal}Andorhal{/link}, {link:sorrow-hill}Sorrow Hill{/link} and the old farms.
• {b}The {link:cult-of-the-damned}Cult of the Damned{/link}.{/b} Living servants of the Lich King who work among the dead, in Andorhal and in the Scholomance.
• {b}The {link:alliance}Alliance{/link}.{/b} Soldiers of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}, priests, alchemists and agents of {link:si-7}SI:7{/link} at {link:chillwind-camp}Chillwind Camp{/link}.
• {b}The {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}.{/b} The garrison of the {link:the-bulwark}Bulwark{/link}, who hold the border for {link:sylvanas-windrunner}the Dark Lady{/link}.
• {b}The {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link}.{/b} Knights, priests and inquisitors of {link:hearthglen}Hearthglen{/link}, and the workers of the lumber mill they seized at Northridge.
• {b}The {link:argent-dawn}Argent Dawn{/link}.{/b} Officers and defenders stationed in both camps.
• {b}The restless dead of the old kingdom.{/b} Ghosts who were never part of the Scourge: the spirits of {link:caer-darrow}Caer Darrow{/link}, the woman of {link:felstone-field}Felstone Field{/link}, the mourners of Sorrow Hill.
• {b}Plague-ridden beasts.{/b} Wolves, bears, bats and vultures, sick with the same plague as the land.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Kingdom.{/b} For generations these were the farmlands and river towns of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}, rich and peaceful behind the strength of the kingdom.
• {b}The {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.{/b} When the orcish {link:horde}Horde{/link} invaded the north, the knights of the Silver Hand rode out against it. {link:tirion-fordring}Tirion Fordring{/link} was among them. After the war he ruled the lands around {link:hearthglen}Hearthglen{/link}, until he was stripped of them for sparing the life of an {link:orcs}orc{/link}.
• {b}The Plague.{/b} Before the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, agents of the {link:cult-of-the-damned}Cult of the Damned{/link} tainted the grain in the granaries of {link:ruins-of-andorhal}Andorhal{/link}, and the grain went out to the villages of the north. Those who ate it sickened, died and rose again as servants of the Lich King. Prince {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas Menethil{/link} came to Andorhal and slew the cult's master, {link:kel-thuzad}Kel'Thuzad{/link}, but the plague had already spread beyond any cure, and the north fell one town at a time.
• {b}The {link:fall-of-lordaeron}Fall of Lordaeron{/link}.{/b} After Arthas murdered his father, the Silver Hand was broken. {link:uther-the-lightbringer}Uther the Lightbringer{/link} died at his student's hand, and a tomb was raised to his memory in these lands. The Barovs of {link:caer-darrow}Caer Darrow{/link} gave their keep to the cult, and the Scholomance was founded in its crypts.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} The {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} holds the heart of the land. The living cling to its edges, and the Crusade holds the north.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Plaguelands",
			text = [=[• The watches of {link:ruins-of-andorhal}Andorhal{/link}, and the great clock on the ruin of its town hall, all stopped at the same hour. It was the hour when the plague first took the city.
• On the island of {link:caer-darrow}Caer Darrow{/link}, the ghosts of the townsfolk are said to live their last happy day over and over, as if nothing had happened to them.
• The {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} and the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} both say they will take Andorhal. Neither says what it will do with the city once it is taken.
• Among the dead of {link:sorrow-hill}Sorrow Hill{/link} lie many who fell defending {link:darrowshire}Darrowshire{/link}, to the east.]=],
